      {
        "id": 36016,
        "name": "broccoli",
        "username": "broccoli",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-06T18:26:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;The_Densetsu&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"The_Densetsu\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Strike<br>\nPower: Deal 1 target 1 damage.<br>\nYou may discard cards from your hand to increase this damage by 1 per card discarded.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Hmm, then we come back to that same problem of “It’s strictly better than his base power.”  Maybe if it was</p>\n<p>Strike<br>\nPower: Discard any number of cards. Deal X damage to 1 target where X is the number of cards discarded.</p>\n<p>Then you could still discard 0 cards once you have some buffs out, but you could also discard a ton when you needed it.  Hmmm, I really like that actually.</p>",
