        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/2acd7d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-06T20:28:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Christopher&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Christopher\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Mr. Fixer is 85.</p>\n<p>Expatriette is 22.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Okay, then I expect he is experienced enough to change his stance more often then he tends to.<br>\nWhile I get that tools go back to hand because they are in his tool box, wouldn’t it have made more sense for stances to instead. The way it plays now, he can have some difficulty changing his fighting style,  but he has plenty of tools (depending on the draw).</p>",
